Subject: [PATCH] cmake: recognise Substrate and give it the netbsd audio backend

SDL_DetectCMakePlatform() had no case for Substrate, so a cross build with
CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME=Substrate fell through to "unknown" and set no platform
variable.  Most of the build still worked, because the big platform branch
keys on CMake's UNIX (which Platform/Substrate sets by deferring to
Platform/Linux) -- X11 video, pthreads and dlopen all came out right.  Two
things did not:

  - Audio: the driver chain starts `if(NETBSD)`, so substrate got no audio
    backend at all despite having a NetBSD-compatible audio(4) /dev/audio.
  - OSS: SDL_OSS_DEFAULT is ON for any UNIX_SYS that is not Linux/NetBSD/
    OpenBSD, so substrate defaulted to an OSS backend it has no /dev/dsp
    for.

Add the platform case and use it in both places.  Substrate is spelled as
its own platform rather than mapped onto Linux because it is not Linux --
it has no evdev, no ALSA and no OSS -- and pretending otherwise is how the
build ends up compiling drivers that cannot work.

--- a/cmake/sdlplatform.cmake
+++ b/cmake/sdlplatform.cmake
@@ -30,6 +30,8 @@
     set(sdl_cmake_platform RISCOS)
   elseif(VITA)
     set(sdl_cmake_platform Vita)
+  elseif(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "Substrate.*")
+    set(sdl_cmake_platform Substrate)
   elseif(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES ".*Linux")
     set(sdl_cmake_platform Linux)
   elseif(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "kFreeBSD.*")
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -211,7 +211,7 @@
   set(SDL_SHARED_AVAILABLE OFF)
 endif()
 
-if((RISCOS OR UNIX_SYS) AND NOT (LINUX OR NETBSD OR OPENBSD))
+if((RISCOS OR UNIX_SYS) AND NOT (LINUX OR NETBSD OR OPENBSD OR SUBSTRATE))
   set(SDL_OSS_DEFAULT ON)
 else()
   set(SDL_OSS_DEFAULT OFF)
@@ -1794,7 +1794,7 @@
   endif()
 
   if(SDL_AUDIO)
-    if(NETBSD)
+    if(NETBSD OR SUBSTRATE)
         set(SDL_AUDIO_DRIVER_NETBSD 1)
         sdl_glob_sources(
           "${SDL3_SOURCE_DIR}/src/audio/netbsd/*.c"
